# Vercel uploads the *working directory*, not the git tree, so .gitignore rules
# do not keep files out of a deployment. Without this file the CLI uploads
# everything on disk — which reached 2.1 GB and failed the build with
# "File size limit exceeded (100 MB)" (Vercel rejects any single file > 100 MB).
#
# The cause was tools/moneyprinterturbo/, a bundled video tool unrelated to the
# tuition app: a ~2 GB Python .venv plus a nested .git. It is already gitignored
# but was still being packaged.
#
# Keep this list to things that are (a) regenerable, (b) never needed at
# runtime by the Next.js app, and (c) big. Anything under public/ that the app
# actually serves must NOT be listed here.

# Unrelated bundled tooling + its virtualenv and nested repo.
tools/
_tools_stash/

# Local build/cache output.
.next/
node_modules/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Test + diagnostic artefacts.
.scene-preview/
*.log

# Agent/session scratch state.
.agents/
.workbuddy-ai/

# Local env files — never ship secrets to a deployment.
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
